{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>על עמו</b> — ayin with a crooked crown (עיי\"ן עקומה). Says: seventy souls came down here and already multiplied from them."], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {0 "The phrase עיי\"ן עקומה (\"crooked ayin\") refers to a masoretic letter-form anomaly on the ע of על in this verse; the reading 'seventy souls came down here and already multiplied from them' likely alludes to Genesis 46:27."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:11:36.838283964Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}